diff --git a/docs/terminal-size-probe.md b/docs/terminal-size-probe.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aa5a118
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/terminal-size-probe.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Optional pre-session terminal size
+
+The Telnet proxy can query a capable serial terminal after it selects an allowed
+BBS destination, before opening the BBS TCP connection. Set
+`telnet.terminalSizeProbeTimeoutMs` to an integer1..10000 to opt in. Omit it or
+set0 to retain fixed `terminalRows`/`terminalCols` and emit no size query.
+Existing configuration, aliases and modem/SIP/audio settings are unchanged.
+
+The proxy sends CSI18t once, accepts the bounded CSI8;rows;columns t response,
+and supplies the dimensions to TelnetCodec's existing NAWS negotiation. The
+peer must still negotiate NAWS; this does not prove its application resized.
+Only this pre-session owner parses size replies. BBS output, binary uploads and
+downloads remain opaque, including size-looking bytes and all256 byte values.
+
+The owner retains up to1024 bytes of ordinary typing, handles split CRLF, and
+forwards that input once TCP connects. Timeout, malformed reserved response,
+invalid nonzero configuration or overflow closes the modem session without
+opening TCP. Cancellation and stale socket/deadline events cannot reopen a
+closed or newer connection. A later call may query again; a failed query is not
+retried in the same call. There is no wire nonce or authentication.
+
+Use the option only with terminals that implement the response, such as the
+reviewed source-built PCPlus candidate. Fixed geometry remains appropriate for
+other terminals. Production enablement requires separate call-path testing.
+
+## Tests and provenance
+
+Run `node --test test/telnet/*.test.js`. The size tests use the actual source
+with declared config/socket/clock boundaries and a real loopback TCP case.
+Default absent/zero output is compared with golden bytes recorded from the
+pre-patch TelnetProxy at f0e8d5f, SHA256
+8ba4a0e1b9d4be1c51bc6d2f534e56e37528eed2d1915e58505fc2be88d99628.
+The configuration fixture contains no private addresses or SIP credentials.
+
+This integrates the GPL-2.0-or-later menu-size patch maintained in bstar's
+PCPlus reconstruction, preserving SynthModem attribution and COPYING. It does
+not claim that SIP/audio/DSP code was reconstructed from PCPlus.
+
+The independent heartbeat fixture also exposed an existing behavior bug:
+ignored RX noise repeatedly postponed a configured menu TX keepalive. RX noise
+now leaves an already-armed deadline intact; actual output, including local
+echo, still defers it. A pre-patch fixture run fails the RX test. Heartbeats
+remain disabled when configured off, and never run while proxying BBS data.
+These tests establish timer/byte behavior, not a physical modem resynchronization
+claim. Backend/session and physical SIP/audio acceptance remain separate.
